{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>They surrounded me</b> — <b>they are extinguished</b> is like \"his lamp is extinguished\" (דעך נרו)." "<b>Like fire of thorns</b> — it does not stand, for it is immediately extinguished."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {0 "The Hebrew cites ידעך נרו, drawing the comparison to דועכו; I read the quoted phrase as a biblical parallel (cf. Job 18:5, יאבד אור רשעים וידעך נרו)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:59.990406751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}